inline_comments.body:
The tests in this PR mock `flash_attn_varlen_func` and the AITER producer, so nothing checks numerics end to end. That's why the descale problem above got through. Please add GPU tests (skipped unless CDNA4 + AITER) that:
- run the real producer against a GemmaRMSNorm + RoPE native reference (BF16 Q/K/gate, descales, dequantized FP8 Q/K/V);
- run FP8 `flash_attn_varlen_func` with the producer's descales, sliced the way the backend slices them, against BF16 attention on the dequantized values;
- parametrize over the per-rank heads of the target models at TP1-TP8 (32/2, 16/2, 16/1, 8/1, 4/1, 2/1) and over batch layouts: one prefill, several prefills, decodes before prefills, 256 sequences, padded rows.

Also, the `hd128` case doesn't exercise anything: the path requires head size 256.

@simondanielsson 

So I prototyped keeping this out of core: `backend.py` and `attention.py` stay unchanged, and a model-specific `PrequantizedQKVAttention(Attention)` owns its own custom op that calls a method that exists only on the AITER FA impl. So far everything looks green: it passes the gfx950 unit/numerics tests and serves Qwen3.5-397B TP2 with FP8 KV, torch.compile and piecewise CUDA graphs with coherent output. Minor downside is that it costs of about 60 duplicated lines of `Attention.forward` and one `_attention_ops` entry in `compilation.py`.

My ask, before I continue any further: would you prefer this over the current API change? In case you would agree, I'll push it as a follow-up commit and run GSM8K plus new serving numbers.
